{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/654250-translation-guide-question","id":654250,"title":"Translation guide question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-06T12:44:43-07:00","id":654250,"title":"Translation guide question","content":"As one player plans on playing a fallen in a descent game I've just read through the conversion rules again and stumbled over cover........<br /> In fallen the demons only have 1 cover so to say and then switch bodies voluntarily or unvoluntarily and usually don't come back (with the &quot;cover&quot; still existing afterwards in whatever state it was before). <br /> <br /> As the converted demons seemingly also have a cover rating are there any rules there for this? Or you just use the normal fallen rules and if the cover rating falls to 0 you are better giving up this host body for good and try to stem against the abyss to get a new host? (aka leave body and try to get into the next)<br /> <br /> or am I mistaken there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T13:27:25-07:00","id":654334,"title":"","content":"This could be done a few different ways, depending on how you intend to incorporate the Fallen into your game's cosmology. Are they completely unrelated in origin to the Unchained, similar to how Kindred clans in Requiem may be convergent evolution of different monsters towards similar outcomes? Are they some different form that can result from the Fall of an angel of the God-Machine? Are they and the God-Machine related, but indirectly?<br /> <br /> Fallen demons converted into the nWoD system don't have a Cover rating. They have an Integrity rating from which they derive their Torment. If they're cosmologically unrelated, I'd stick with that: the Fallen aren't of the same substance as the angels of the God-Machine, so they don't risk metaphysical discovery without the protection of Cover the way the Unchained do. The God-Machine could find out about them and come after them the same way it could do so to a mage or a werewolf, but compromise risks don't occur.<br /> <br /> Even if the Fallen in your game are similar enough to be subject to the risk of discovery and get pulled into the spy genre, a player who wants to play one of the Fallen probably is interested in the different way the Fallen obtain human bodies. If you want to combine the possession/merging with a human host exhibited by the Fallen with the espionage of Descent and the idea of compromise, I wrote up a variant of the Unchained for another player in my game that attempts to do exactly that. I'll post it separately for space/organization purposes. It can easily be adapted for Fallen mechanics (substitute temporary Faith for Aether and permanent Faith for Primum) and cosmology (instead of being Burned while ephemeral, the character must obtain a body before running out of temporary Faith, or else return to the Abyss).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T13:36:51-07:00","id":654343,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Incubators</b></span><br /> <br /> Not all of the Unchained are fallen angels; not truly. Strange events occasionally cause an angel to share in the essence of another type of being. Spirits from the Shadow Realm feed upon angelic essence from a project near a spirit locus. An angel is infected by a sympathetic contagion rising into the world from a weak and foul place. Sometimes the God-Machine itself attempts to induce these conditions, capturing a foreign being and implanting angelic organs within it to subvert its nature. Some of the resulting hybrid angels, in turn, inherit the capacity to Fall. They become twice-subverted, estranged adoptees: the Incubators.<br /> <br /> <i>folded up for length:</i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Ephemeral Demons</b></span><br /> <br /> In his natural state, an Incubator exists as an ephemeral being in Twilight. He is much like an angel, even composed of angelic ephemera. He is not an angel, however, and his traits differ considerably. Treat the character as a demon in demonic form, with all of the same traits and abilities as normal, but with the following exceptions:<br /> <br /> <i>Manifestation:</i> In his natural state, the demon possesses the Twilight Form Manifestation, and can be perceived and touched by angels in Twilight (or characters using abilities that could similarly perceive or touch angels). The demon also possesses the Incubate Manifestation; see below.<br /> <br /> <i>Aetheric Bleed:</i> Every hour spent in Twilight drains one point of Aether. Entering Twilight Form does not restore Aether like adopting demonic form normally, and the demon may not roll to recover Aether if he runs out.<br /> <br /> <i>Corpus:</i> The Incubator's Health trait becomes Corpus. It remains Stamina + Size, but the Incubator heals all non-aggravated damage from corporeal injury.<br /> <br /> <i>Burned:</i> Incubators in Twilight Form are Burned until they can merge with a new host.<br /> <br /> <i>Incubate:</i> This Manifestation may only be used on mortal humans with weakened or loosened souls. The ephemeral Incubator can reflexively sense any such targets within a half-mile radius. Valid targets include humans who have lost their soul, but also include the comatose, the sickly or dying, those broken by supernatural powers, or other cases by Storyteller adjudication.<br /> <br /> Once the demon locates a potential host and travels to her, overlaying his ephemera on top of her body, he may spend one Aether as an instant action, contesting Resolve + Presence versus the potential host's Resolve + Composure. He may spend additional Aether to add 3 dice each. If the demon fails, he must wait one hour before trying again on the same potential host. If he succeeds, he merges with the new host, exiting ephemeral form and gaining Hold over his new identity.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Wearing the Flesh</b></span><br /> <br /> An Incubator has no Cover and cannot develop it, even when nested within a host. He cannot accumulate multiple hosts at a given time, invoke a Legend, or obtain facades or relationships from demonic pacts. He receives normal beats instead of Cover beats. He can still sign soul pacts, in which case the signatory becomes a valid target to Incubate; no roll is made, and the merger occurs as per an exceptional success. He can still Spoof, and substitute the security of his host for his Supernatural Tolerance. The trait he uses to do these things instead of Cover is called Hold.<br /> <br /> On incubating within a host, the demon gains a Hold rating equal to 5 plus the number of net successes by which he beat his host on the successful Incubate contest, to a maximum of 10. Hold represents the integration of the demon into his new host body. Hold cannot be purchased with experiences, though it increases by one dot for every week the demon spends within the same host without adopting ephemeral form. If the demon should choose to &quot;drop the body,&quot; taking an instant action to split into a dead host body and a freed ephemeral demon, or if the body should die from non-aggravated wounds, he loses his Hold rating and must start over with another host.<br /> <br /> Hold is more rigid in nature than Cover, less easily bent but more easily broken. An Incubator within a host does not risk compromise for acting out of character or revealing his true nature. Other compromise risks, such as those for Exploits or adopting demonic form, still apply, however, and they are more threatening. On a failed compromise roll, instead of losing a dot of Cover, the demon must roll his Primum and lose dots of Hold equal to the number of successes rolled. Reaching Hold 0 breaks down the synthesis, as if the demon had dropped the body.<br /> <br /> Fusing with a host, unlike stepping into a Cover, integrates some of the host's memories: short-term memory going back for the past 24 hours, and long-term memory about important relationships and emotionally treasured assets. Often the integration alters the Incubator's personality to more closely resemble the new host's, and the demon's player may choose to alter his Virtue or Vice accordingly. For every point of starting Hold above 5, he may even choose to reassign a Skill dot to another Skill within the same category (Physical, Mental or Social), or to do the same with an Attribute dot within the same category, or a Merit dot. The new dots represent the host's physical or mental traits overwriting the demon's to some degree.<br /> <br /> The demon may adopt demonic form without leaving the host and dropping the body, as per normal demons. The integrated host body is physically transformed by the demon's Primum. The Incubator can then return to his normal host's form like a normal demon switching Covers.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}